  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling Emergency nutrition and health response for conflict affected children fleeing war in Sudan to South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In consultation and coordination with UNOCHA, RRC, the clusters, and local authorities, Cordaid/ADA will target the most vulnerable. The primary beneficiaries will include Pregnant mothers (protects maternal health and nutritional status, promotes optimal growth of child in womb, helps ensure adequate birth weight); mothers of children 0-23 months (Helps ensure adequate breast milk, protects maternal health and nutritional status); all children 0-23 months (Protects child growth during a critical period of physical development, Protects health of child when s/he is also at high risk of infection and death); and HH of participating women and children (Supplements household food supply and improves household food security, Encourages program participation, Discourages sharing of the individual ration).
&#x2022;	Pregnant and lactating mothers
&#x2022;	children 0-23 months.
&#x2022;	Households with SAM/MAM cases.
This total number of beneficiaries is based on cluster recommended  average household size of 6 persons per Household.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the start of the conflict in Sudan in the month of April of 2023, nearly 300,000 (60% are children) people have sought refuge into South Sudan, 90% of whom are South Sudanese nationals. As the fighting continues to rage on, more people are expected to seek refuge in South Sudan particularly through boarder points of Renk and Rotriak in Unity State. Yet, South Sudan is facing high humanitarian needs driven by the economic decline, especially depreciation of its currency, conflict and insecurity, climatic shocks such as flooding and long dry spells, and failed and/or low agricultural production in this calendar year.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To provide emergency health and nutrition assistance to 6,000 children and pregnant/lactating mothers who fled the conflict in Sudan and are in South Sudan.</narrative>
  </description>
